{title: The Old Account}
{key: C}
{x_theme: praise, faith-trust, blood}
{x_source: chrd:the_old_account.chrd}

{comment: Verse 1}
[C]There was a time on earth, when in the book of Heav'n
[F]An old account was [C]standing for [G7]sins yet unforgiv'n;
[C]My name was at the top, and many things below,
[F]I went unto the [C]Keeper, and [G7]settled long [C]ago.

{comment: Refrain}
[G7]Long ago (down on my knees), [C]long ago (I settled it all),
[C]Yes, the old account was [D7]settled long [G7]ago (Hallelujah!);
[C]And the record's clear today, for He [F]washed my sins [C]away,
[C]When the old account was [G7]settled long [C]ago.

{comment: Verse 2}
[C]The old account was large, and growing every day,
[F]For I was always sin[C]ning, and ne[G7]ver tried to pay;
[C]But when I looked ahead, and saw such pain and woe,
[F]I said that I would [C]settle, I [G7]settled long [C]ago.

{comment: Verse 3}
[C]When in that happy home, my Savior's home above,
[F]I'll sing redemption's [C]story, and [G7]praise Him for His love;
[C]I'll not forget that book, with pages white as snow,
[F]Because I came and [C]settled, and [G7]settled long [C]ago.

{comment: Verse 4}
[C]O sinner, trust the Lord, be cleansed of all your sin,
[F]For thus He hath provi[C]ded for you [G7]to enter in;
[C]And then if you should live a hundred years below,
[F]Up there you'll not [C]regret it, [G7]you settled [C]long ago.
